    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13282" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονέομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go away, depart,</i> freq in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, only in pres. (sts. with fut. sense,
			as <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.113
			</span></i>) and impf., always at the end of the line, with
			the first syll. long, metri gr., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονέεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 l. c., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονέωνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονέοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.313
				</span></i>
			, al.</div>
